type: software
title: "Research Office: an offline 3D research office with a mode-of-entry board for International Business teaching"
abstract: >-
  A self-contained, bilingual (Vietnamese–English) 3D research office that runs
  entirely in the browser. The visitor walks through a single room and speaks
  with six characters: the author, and five fictional characters carried over
  from the knowledge-estate scene of the author's academic homepage. Every
  answer is written in advance by the author and stored in the page; nothing is
  generated at run time and the page makes no network request of any kind once
  loaded, apart from the one audio file a visitor may choose to play, which is
  served from the repository itself. A mode-of-entry board on the right-hand
  wall sets out seven entry
  modes, from exporting to foreign direct investment, each anchored to a
  standard International Business theory — the Uppsala model, transaction-cost
  economics, agency theory, the CAGE framework, the resource-based view, the
  born-global perspective, and Dunning's OLI paradigm. It is used as open
  teaching material for an undergraduate International Business course. Built
  from plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript with three.js; no build step, no
  server-side component, no analytics and no third-party request.
